Subject: [PATCH 0007/0012] hand input to the game and own the connection

A cloud game needs relative motion, not a pointer that stops at the screen
edge: the stream window turns the mouse into relative events the host asks for,
switches the window once per F11 press, and drops a frame the compositor cannot
take instead of blocking the producer. The stream window also gets its own
Wayland connection, so the render thread and the interface never dispatch each
other's events (the shared connection made the driver see a second release
fence).

Upstream-Status: Inappropriate [STM32MP25 performance work]

